        "at": "2026-11-02T00:04:59"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "MEASURED",
      "narration_text": "I tested eight of them, like read, which can be reed or red, each in a sentence that makes its meaning clear. Sixteen sentences, ten right. Only two words came out right both ways. Last night I read a book comes out with reed, not red. There's no grammar check behind it, only a few clues from the word just before.",
